{"t": "2026-10-14T14:06:12", "stage": "C3", "verb": "log", "args": ["Explanation shelf, read whole (verified): Felin and Zenger (2017). Claims that bear here: economic actors' theories (questions, problems, contrarian beliefs) direct perception and reveal value (pp. 260-263); organizations grant some actors' theories power, aid their composition, and attract those who share the theory by self-selection (p. 265); hierarchy decides when discussion does not (Simon, quoted p. 265). First reading: a candidate contradiction on what settles what a room acts on (a chosen theory against the topic's given picture), and a resemblance in self-selection to a starter's proposal. Next: Felin and Zenger (2016)."], "opts": {"kind": "note"}, "offset": 0, "limit": 80, "lines": 1, "total": 1, "refused": null}
