{"t": "2026-10-14T14:06:31", "stage": "C3", "verb": "log", "args": ["Explanation shelf, read whole (verified): Felin and Zenger (2016, SSRN manuscript pages). Claims that bear here: a firm's theory reveals an architecture and bundle of problems to solve, and guides which to solve itself and which to leave to others (pp. 4-5, 11); serendipitous need-solution pairs are others' priced solutions (p. 8); even recognizing a solution needs a theory (p. 14). First reading: with the 2017 paper, a candidate contradiction on what settles a room's work; the room's goal (a picture) is mostly given, not composed as a contrarian theory. Next: O'Mahony and Ferraro (2007)."], "opts": {"kind": "note"}, "offset": 0, "limit": 80, "lines": 1, "total": 1, "refused": null}
