{"t": "2026-10-14T14:07:17", "stage": "C3", "verb": "log", "args": ["Explanation shelf, read whole (verified): O'Mahony and Ferraro (2007). Claims that bear here: 'Before an organization can develop a form of governance, it must establish a shared basis of authority' (p. 1081); Debian ran five years on de facto founder rule, recalled an autocratic second leader, then wrote a constitution with positional authority limited by democratic means (pp. 1088-1090); members came to elect organization builders, and face-to-face ties predicted the leadership team (pp. 1091, 1098). First reading: a contradiction with the model's claim that rooms organized almost without decided order; the likely resolution is the setting (73 hours against 13 years), to be decided from the record. Next: Bechky (2006)."], "opts": {"kind": "note"}, "offset": 0, "limit": 80, "lines": 1, "total": 1, "refused": null}
