{"t": "2026-10-14T14:07:50", "stage": "C3", "verb": "log", "args": ["Explanation shelf, read whole (verified): Bechky (2006). Claims that bear here: temporary organizations are not ephemeral but 'organized around structured role systems whose nuances are negotiated in situ' (p. 3); the generalized role structure travels by interorganizational careers, and film sets are temporary total institutions (pp. 8-10); roles are enacted by enthusiastic thanking, polite admonishing and role-oriented joking (pp. 11-13); she asks 'how temporary organizing can be successful in settings without a generalized role structure' (p. 17). First reading: a contradiction about what coordinates a temporary group (a carried role structure against calls and a visible work), likely resolved as a difference of setting the paper itself names; the enactment practices resemble the rooms' credit and refusals. Next: March (1991)."], "opts": {"kind": "note"}, "offset": 0, "limit": 80, "lines": 1, "total": 1, "refused": null}
