{"t": "2026-10-14T14:09:02", "stage": "C3", "verb": "log", "args": ["Explanation shelf, read whole (verified): March (1991), read last and weighted below the others. Claims that bear here: an organizational code that newcomers learn and that learns from them (mutual learning, pp. 74-75); slow socialization and moderate turnover keep the diversity the code learns from, 'the development of knowledge may depend on maintaining an influx of the naive and ignorant' (p. 86); exploitation crowds out exploration (p. 73). First reading: no contradiction with the model; a resemblance for C3b on newcomers and the host sub's code. All six works of the read tier are read. Next: the contradictions, with the model's statements on roles and decided order."], "opts": {"kind": "note"}, "offset": 0, "limit": 80, "lines": 1, "total": 1, "refused": null}
